<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-QBE half year net profit rises.</title>
<headline>RTRS-QBE half year net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to December 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    107.8 vs 112.8</p>
<p>    Net					85.4 vs 83.0</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cents)	   9.0  vs 7.2</p>
<p>NOTE: QBE Insurance Group Ltd is an insurance company. The company said the results conform with industry accounting standards, but it releases separate accounts not including unrealised gains and losses on investments. The company said the previous year's dividend had been adjusted for last September's one-for-four bonus issue.  </p>
<p>    Sales (gross earned premium)    840.9 vs 740.5</p>
<p>    Other income			  243.1 vs 228.7</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    29.1 vs 30.1</p>
<p>Dividend is 50 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date April 4</p>
<p>Reg date March 7</p>
<p>    Tax					15.2 vs 12.1</p>
<p>    Interest				  5.3 vs 4.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    5.2 vs 4.2</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
